; The xor of two bytes extracted from a vector matches the h-register
; __builtin_parity idiom (xor(trunc(x), trunc(srl(x, 8)))). Previously this was
; lowered to the GR8_NOREX XOR8rr_NOREX instruction whose result could be
; allocated to a high-byte register (e.g. %bh). Because the xor result is used
; here (zero-extended into a GR32/GR64 register that may require a REX prefix),
; the encoder failed with "Cannot encode high byte register in REX-prefixed
; instruction". The h-register trick must only be used when the xor value
; result is dead and only EFLAGS are consumed.

